{"kind":"artifact","text":"Implementation report for explicit state@3 request authoring (request 65fa914a) at exact head 21341300c77c499e3a5b59c204ee7156de57760d on request/explicit-request-authoring, one commit over current main 183211c3, forty-nine changed paths, no ui or embed change, fulfilling my promise 07a271e5. What it does: (1) every request-lifecycle state reaching app.buildActRequest is signed workroom/state@3 and must state exactly one result; the caller names target_ref, the boundary fills target_repo with the workroom genesis id and reads target_head from the ref with git show-ref --verify at filing; a caller-supplied target_repo or target_head is refused outright, distinct from a release report's target_pre_head, which is untouched. (2) The body-local half of the judgement is the exported workroom.ReadRequestChoice, which the fold's decideRequestResult now calls, so surfaces refuse exactly the shapes the fold refuses in the same words; the ancestry walk and roster read stay in the fold, and all existing fold refusal strings are preserved. Missing, mixed, malformed, foreign-repo, non-branch and unresolvable choices refuse before signing, so the frontier does not move. (3) One path serves gs state, gs batch entries, the MCP state tool and the resident POST /v0/act. The guarded reassign-if-unclaimed replacement is filed under the new workroom/reassign-if-unclaimed@1 and states its own result; nothing is inherited from the retired request, so gs reassign-if-unclaimed gains --body and the MCP tool gains body. (4) kernel.PriorAct returns the act already accepted under an actor's idempotency key from the dedup index Submit consults; reproduceAcceptedTarget rebuilds the request from that act's own triple and uses it only when byte-identical to the accepted signed intent, so an exact retry after the ref moved replays and a fresh key measures the current ref; no new state machine or retry cache. (5) state@2 and reassign-if-unclaimed@0 bytes and interpretation a